    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "da7b0f89-257c-3f0b-bca7-8a33f5aedb56",
                "word": "EFF",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a21a118e-10cb-36f3-8295-903f4050ad6d",
                        "entry_id": "da7b0f89-257c-3f0b-bca7-8a33f5aedb56",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of Electronic Frontier Foundation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Internet",
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "initialism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cb7eace-d066-48e6-b99f-f3355037e7b1",
                                "sense_id": "a21a118e-10cb-36f3-8295-903f4050ad6d",
                                "text": "The EFF asked Legere about the issue on Twitter. After partially answering the question in a video, Legere said, \"Who the f— are you anyway EFF? Why are you stirring up so much trouble, and who pays you?\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "566c6cd9-ea4c-3c3a-b3e8-fd1f675fbf01",
                        "entry_id": "da7b0f89-257c-3f0b-bca7-8a33f5aedb56",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Initialism of Economic Freedom Fighters."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "South-Africa",
                            "abbreviation",
                            "alt-of",
                            "initialism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5cc5257-7167-4205-8b06-986c0b34ed1d",
                                "sense_id": "566c6cd9-ea4c-3c3a-b3e8-fd1f675fbf01",
                                "text": "Once all the votes are counted, if the ANC remains below 50% it will be forced to enter a coalition with one or more parties. Depending on how low its support dips, it may need to form a deal with one of the larger opposition parties such as the DA or EFF to remain in power."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "c8ae997d-172a-39c2-86d8-0f5c7bfd8c0f",
                "word": "eff",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8c055f42-44bc-4da8-8040-542908536cfb",
                        "entry_id": "c8ae997d-172a-39c2-86d8-0f5c7bfd8c0f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "effs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d5703dce-4738-3ac9-9a63-993a842a04a5",
                        "entry_id": "c8ae997d-172a-39c2-86d8-0f5c7bfd8c0f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative spelling of ef; the name of the Latin-script letter F/f."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b8f2109-1372-4dfb-8aea-3acab716c5c8",
                                "sense_id": "d5703dce-4738-3ac9-9a63-993a842a04a5",
                                "text": "Why against printers all this noise? This summoning of blackguard boys? Why so sagacious in your guesses? Your effs, and tees, and arrs, and eſſes? Take my advice; to make you safe, I know a shorter way be half."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d4148e6-14d6-426f-8c5e-934891b12d69",
                                "sense_id": "d5703dce-4738-3ac9-9a63-993a842a04a5",
                                "text": "‘Eff. You. En,’ said Mr Banstead. ‘Fun![…]’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ebeafae-7d4c-4fcc-9436-7b4984a90d2b",
                                "sense_id": "d5703dce-4738-3ac9-9a63-993a842a04a5",
                                "text": "A or an? When an indefinite article precedes an acronym or initialism, the choice between a and an follows from the pronunciation: / a FAQ file (“fack”; but “an FAQ file” with the alternate pronunciation “eff-ay-cue”) / an FTC commissioner (“eff-tee-cee”)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c61192b8-19f3-4c02-bd19-656ec2412a1a",
                                "sense_id": "d5703dce-4738-3ac9-9a63-993a842a04a5",
                                "text": "‘S-S-C…sitting on a tree…eff-you-cee-kay-i-en-ji.’"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
